  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1241 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nThe cold rain comes to an end on Tuesday evening and set the local \narea for a cooler Wednesday morning with lows in the low 30s across \nthe southern Edwards Plateau and Hill Country and mid 30s elsewhere. \nThis is the first opportunity for these areas to get to the freezing \nmark for the fall season. A Freeze Warning likely issue for these \nlocations sometime Tuesday if this trend continues. \n\nWednesday will be cool with highs in the 50s and 60s across the \nlocal area with sunny skies and light northerly winds for the most \npart. The Wednesday night into Thursday morning period is looking \nsimilar to Wednesday morning but with a shift into the I-35 corridor \nwith clear skies and light to calm winds. With this type of setup, \nthe Thanksgiving Day morning is shaping to be a cold one for a good \nportion of the local area. A Freeze Warning likely issue for those \nareas. As a friendly reminder, our office issues Freeze Warnings to \nhighlight agriculture impacts and only to highlight the first freeze \nof the season. Once a county has met this criteria, it is removed \nfrom the Freeze program for the winter season. The only exception \nwill be if a late freeze occurs once the growing season has already \nstarted. Thanksgiving Day's high temperatures range from the mid to \nupper 50s to low 60s.\n\nDry weather is forecast for the rest of the week including the \nupcoming weekend with a slow warmup Friday but back to the 70s for \nSaturday and Sunday.",
